  "details": "It would be nice to have the possibility to read certain stuff from currently active avatars in the instance per user from the API.\n\nLike for example their texture memory,contactpoints,lightscources etc. Currently we do have an ingame option for this, but this can become extremely tedious to do so if you are moderating a bigger instance, Ofcourse there are also settings to do certain stuff in this regard like limiting download size etc, but if you have a pc that can barely keep up and you show people manually this also becomes extremely annoying. Plus this also doesnt help with other data like lightscources/contactpoint/triangles.\n\nThis information of avi's isnt really secret anyways since you can just read them once you are in the instance, so why is it not a feature already?\n\nSo having an api reading of this so ppl can make moderation tools themselves would be amazing and take off a lot of work from our hands.",
